From 1eaf4954596fd01925c160ad9c3d6f6902829ac7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abito <33889084+abitocodes@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:26:21 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Retrain PSF models from the Korail survey, one survey
 item per feature

The original models ignored items the survey respondents clearly react
to, for two reasons:
- two-option items were trained as 0/1 but the web form sends 0/2, so
  'low availability' reached the model as an unseen value;
- F.2/F.4/F.6/F.8 merged 2-3 items into one GMM cluster feature, which
  dropped one item of each pair (e.g. equipment usability).

config/catboost_config.py now uses every survey item as its own
categorical feature for all eight PSFs, and models/*.cbm are retrained
on all 26,416 answers of 396 Korail workers with the values the fixed
form sends (same hyper-parameters as before: 500 iterations, depth 6,
learning rate 0.05). The GMM bundles are no longer used and removed.

Checked on 79 held-out respondents (models trained without them):
accuracy 57.6% vs 56.5% for the old models as deployed (difference not
significant; two respondents agree on the same scenario only 38-62% of
the time). Items the respondents react to but the model ignores: 7 -> 0;
items with the reversed direction: 2 -> 0. The app's own
predict_psf_catboost gives the same level as the benchmark for 1,200
test scenarios sent as the form sends them.

F.6 still predicts 'bad' almost always: the survey only asked about
lightning and fog occurring (fixed in the survey app); it needs new
survey data.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
